cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use this software or its released artifacts, please cite the
  repository release below and the accompanying preprint once its arXiv
  identifier is assigned (it will be added here).
title: "Microfluidic Native Physics: Reliability Audits for Machine-Learned Droplet-Microfluidic Design Surrogates — code and artifacts"
type: software
version: "0.3-preprint"
date-released: "2026-10-21"
authors:
  - family-names: Zhang
    given-names: Zhiyuan
repository-code: "https://github.com/LibertychaserUS/microfluidic-native-physics"
url: "https://github.com/LibertychaserUS/microfluidic-native-physics"
abstract: >-
  Code, frozen protocols, deviation registers, number ledger, hash manifests
  and summary artifacts of a retrospective reliability-under-shift study of
  machine-learned surrogates for droplet microfluidics: a sealed chemistry
  holdout, a sealed cross-laboratory validation, a frozen physics-guided
  constrained regressor, an expanded shift audit on public DAFD data and a
  method-matrix benchmark. The results are mostly negative and no wet-lab
  feasibility is claimed.
license: Apache-2.0
keywords:
  - microfluidics
  - droplet generation
  - machine learning
  - distribution shift
  - physics-guided regression
  - applicability domain
  - conformal prediction
  - reproducibility
